{
  "summary": "This experiment tested whether adding a ResNet50 image branch via concat fusion to the best-known RNA configuration (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) improves validation accuracy over the RNA-only baseline, yielding ~0.632 accuracy (F1: ~0.607) compared to ~0.650 (F1: ~0.628) for the RNA-only scvi_n200 setup (llm_summary_005). The slight degradation (~0.019 in accuracy) suggests that in this specific configuration the image branch did not provide a net benefit and may have introduced mild interference, though the small magnitude and the fact that only one fusion strategy (concat) and one image encoder (ResNet50) were tested mean this does not definitively rule out complementary image signal. It remains uncertain whether alternative fusion mechanisms (e.g., attention, gating) or stronger image encoders (e.g., ViT-L) could recover or exceed the RNA-only performance, leaving the broader multimodal design space partially open but currently unsupported by positive evidence."
}

